
=== DRY RUN — No changes will be made ===

--- Console guidance ---
1. Log in to the tenant's Hetzner Cloud Console
2. Create a sub-project named 'tenant-fixture-tenant-prd'
3. Inside the sub-project, go to Security → API Tokens
4. Create a project-scoped API token with Read+Write permissions
5. Copy the token (shown only once)

--- Smoke-test commands (run after token creation) ---
read -rs -p 'Hetzner token: ' HCLOUD_TOKEN; echo
(
  export HCLOUD_TOKEN
  hcloud server create --name 'probe-provision-fixture-tenant' --type cx11 --image ubuntu-22.04 --location nbg1
  hcloud server delete 'probe-provision-fixture-tenant'
)
unset HCLOUD_TOKEN

--- Teardown ---
  Delete sub-project via Console: Projects → tenant-fixture-tenant-prd → Delete
  Revoke the API token: Security → API Tokens → Revoke

Next step: soleur:provision-github fixture-tenant <org> <reviewer>

=== Teardown commands (resources created during this run) ===
  (no resources were created)

If the probe server 'probe-provision-fixture-tenant' was not cleaned up:
  hcloud server delete 'probe-provision-fixture-tenant'

To tear down the Hetzner sub-project:
  Delete via Hetzner Console → Projects → tenant-fixture-tenant-prd → Delete
  (CLI does not support project deletion)
